## Gated delivery (execution discipline)

Each phase is a **gated delivery unit**, not a planning-only milestone:

```text
Architecture → Decisions → Readiness → IMPLEMENTATION AUTHORIZED
→ Build completely → Test (functional/DB/security/browser/responsive/a11y)
→ Adversarial/source/scope audit → Fix in-scope → Evidence + docs
→ PASS / COMPLETE / VERIFIED / LOCKED → only then next phase
```

“Implementation not authorized” is normal during planning — **not** final completion. Do not accumulate next-phase architecture while the current phase is undelivered. Dependent implementation does not start while its predecessor remains conditional.
